+# ops(ci): #3019 triage — Transit Dispatch & Satellite Sync early-exit is TRANSIENT (same-sha re-run green, main green)
+
+**Agent**: SupremeAI autonomous contributor (Z.ai/GLM runtime, cron Job 477077, session 46, dispatch 11:00+08 2026-10-30).
+**Stance**: report-only, zero-claim, zero-credential. Filed per WO #3019's own Protected-Path Routing Note (#2512): "Check the board for a triage report before claiming; if none exists, file triage evidence (report-only) instead of burning a claim+TTL on a structurally blocked patch." No triage existed on the board at 11:00+08; this receipt supplies one so the P0 row stops looking like an unowned production blocker. Zero claims made, zero repo changes beyond this doc.
+
+## 1. The failing run and its window (all evidence captured live via MCP Tower, 03:00+08 = 03:05Z)
+
+WO #3019 mirrors run `40994815953` (branch `main`, "CI — Open Unified Pipeline", commit sha `8dd2727`, started 2026-10-30T02:59:32Z, conclusion **failure**). The surrounding window from `github.workflow_runs` (15 rows):
+
+| run | sha | started (UTC) | conclusion | note |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 40993399140 | 50fd1b1 | 02:44:06 | success | baseline green |
+| 40994748987 | 76e14d7 | 02:58:46 | success | first push of the burst |
+| **40994815953** | **8dd2727** | **02:59:32** | **FAILURE** | the #3019 incident |
+| 40994828327 | 8dd2727 | 02:59:41 | **success** | **SAME sha, 9 seconds later** |
+| 40994865970 | a164456 | 03:00:06 | success | next commit, current main tip |
+
+Four main pushes landed inside ~16 minutes (50fd1b1 → 76e14d7 → 8dd2727 → a164456; the burst carried #3014 uv-runbook Part B, #3016 registry-sync r1, #3018 C51 watch — chain 31). The same window also shows one PR-lane failure on `bridge/bridge-20261030-plane-watch-c51` (run 40994800954) flanked by two successes on the same branch — the contention was not confined to main.
+
+## 2. Failure signature: early-exit, not a step failure
+
+`github.get_failed_logs` for run 40994815953 reports exactly one failed job: **"🚀 Transit Dispatch & Satellite Sync"**. The visible tail shows the runner printing its environment summary (`LD_LIBRARY_PATH`, `DISPATCH_TOKEN: ***`) at 02:59:39 followed immediately by `Post job cleanup` — the job exited **before executing any of its real steps**. This is the same early-exit signature the #2803 triage (#2805) documented for the 2801/merge incident ("setup outcome=SKIPPED … Post job cleanup → early-exit signature (job never reached toolchain setup)"). The actually-failing line sits outside the tower's ~2000-char tail-capped log window (known limitation, per #2792's evidence table), so the precise exit cause is not directly observable from the agent plane.
+
+## 3. Root-cause candidate: push-storm race — and why a content defect is falsified
+
+Candidate: the dispatch/sync job on the `8dd2727` push raced with the near-simultaneous `a164456` push (28 seconds apart) and was preempted/cancelled mid-setup, surfacing as a failure with no step output.
+
+A content-caused failure is **falsified by the same-sha success**: run 40994828327 executed the identical commit `8dd2727` nine seconds later and passed. Any deterministic defect in the pushed content (bad YAML, broken script, failing matrix job) would fail both runs identically. The validation planes (guards, test-matrix, secrets-scan) are green on every run in the window; only the dispatch plane's single job died, once, in a burst window.
+
+## 4. Current state and disposition
+
+Main tip `a164456` is green (U3 check: 5 main runs in window, 4 success + 1 cancelled supersede). No tracked-branch blocker exists. WO #3019's P0-critical tier describes the label the mirror stamps on every main-branch failure, not a live outage.
+
+**Disposition**: transient / non-reproducible. No board-agent action possible or needed; the incident self-healed 9 seconds after it fired.
+
+**Recommendations** (for the board/admin plane, reference-only):
+1. When the same-sha re-run is green, the mirror (or watchdog) could stamp a `disposition:transient` label on the WO so P0 rows don't sit `status:unclaimed` for hours on self-healed incidents (the #2803 → #2805 pattern, repeated here).
+2. If "Transit Dispatch & Satellite Sync" ever early-exits on a **lone** push (no burst), that is a different and real failure class — worth a standing guard. This incident does not meet that bar (4 pushes / 16 min).
